      "text": "39-year-old male presenting with low back pain for 2 months. Character: dull aching pain; radiation: down the left leg; aggravated by long sitting; relieved by hot fomentation. Severity 7/10. Associated: morning stiffness, numbness in the leg. PMH: Hypertension for 9 years; Asthma since childhood. Drugs: Amlodipine 5 mg; Salbutamol inhaler 100 mcg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: hypertension. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
